    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8792" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōcălus</span></b> , i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				mythic king in Sicily</i>, <i>who gave protection
				to Dœdalus when he fled from the persecution of
			Minos</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 8, 261</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 4, 2,
				2</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōcălĭ-des</span></b> ,
			um, f., <i>the daughters of
				Cocalus</i>, <i><span class="en">Sil. 14, 42</span></i>.</div>
